Task: TV4-D16 CommitAdvancer majority/current-term commit rule.
Code commit under test: 7047b07bc857cfa9d8aa36b55d8162f9b08a2708
  feat(raft): add CommitAdvancer majority commit with current-term rule [TV4-D16]
Base commit: e5002965463f5d0334143237ed036b293ceaed92 (TV4-D15 test commit)
No commit was pushed.

Files changed by the D16 commit:
- backend-node/src/main/java/vn/nhom6/railway/raft/replication/CommitAdvancer.java (new)
- backend-node/src/main/java/vn/nhom6/railway/raft/replication/RaftReplicationService.java
    Added Hooks.onMatchIndexAdvanced(String peerId, long matchIndex) as a default
    no-op, invoked after a successful state.advanceMatchIndex(...). The hook is
    additive; existing hook implementations and existing tests are unaffected.
- backend-node/src/test/java/vn/nhom6/railway/raft/replication/CommitSafetyTest.java (new)

Files that were not modified: RaftState, PersistentRaftNode,
AppendEntriesHandler, RaftTransportAdapter, LeaderHeartbeatScheduler,
ReplicationTracker, AppendRetryCoordinator, and all pre-existing tests.

Implemented rule (SPEC-04 section 5):
- Only a LEADER advances commitIndex; a non-leader always returns empty.
- Cluster size = ReplicationTracker snapshot size + 1 (the Leader itself).
- Quorum = size / 2 + 1; for 5 Nodes this is 3.
- Samples are the Leader's lastLogIndex plus every peer matchIndex, sorted
  descending; candidate N is the quorum-th largest value.
- No advance when N <= commitIndex (idempotent, monotonic).
- No direct advance when termAt(N) != currentTerm(); old-term entries can only
  be committed indirectly by a later current-term entry (Figure 8 safety).
- No advance when N > lastLogIndex or when state.advanceCommitIndex refuses.
- Returns OptionalLong of the new commit index, or empty.

