--- 3. Not implemented / not proven (explicit gaps) ---

3.1 CommitAdvancer is not yet wired into the runtime Leader loop. The D16
    change adds the rule, the test suite and the onMatchIndexAdvanced hook; a
    production caller must still invoke CommitAdvancer.advance() on the
    serialized Raft event loop.
3.2 The Leader does not yet deliver newly committed entries to a commit
    listener; no apply notification is emitted by this change.
3.3 No Leader no-op entry is appended on becomeLeader, so entries inherited
    from a previous term still cannot be committed until a current-term entry
    follows them.
3.4 There is no markApplied / BookingStateMachine apply in this change, so
    "Raft-committed" is not yet the same statement as "applied to the booking
    database".
3.5 All validation is FakeNetwork plus RaftState/ReplicationTracker unit
    testing. This run does not prove real TCP replication, five Docker nodes,
    clock/scheduler behavior at real latency, process-crash recovery, or
    PostgreSQL durability of applied bookings.

